@startuml
title ProofSieve | Wallet presentation and evidence recovery
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontColor #15283F
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #526B8A
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #EDF4FC
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #8CA6C9

actor "Scoped verifier" as Caller
participant "ProofSieve Guard" as Guard
participant "Configured verifier\nEUDI or Credo" as Adapter
actor "Wallet" as Wallet
database "Wallet session journal" as Journal
database "Decision evidence" as Evidence

Caller -> Guard: POST to the wallet endpoint\nwith start and operationId
Guard -> Guard: Authorize the exact endpoint
Guard -> Journal: Reserve the caller, endpoint and operation
Guard -> Adapter: Start a presentation transaction
Adapter --> Guard: Transaction and authorization request URI
Guard -> Journal: Bind transaction to the session
Guard --> Caller: HTTP 201 · session, wallet link and expiry
Caller -> Wallet: Open the authorization request
Wallet -> Adapter: Present the requested proof

Caller -> Guard: POST complete with the same caller,\nendpoint, operationId and sessionId
alt Presentation pending
    Guard -> Adapter: Read the bound transaction result
    Adapter --> Guard: Pending
    Guard --> Caller: HTTP 202 · repeat the same completion
else Presentation resolved before expiry
    Guard -> Adapter: Retrieve the bound verification result
    Adapter --> Guard: Checked claims or proof refusal
    Guard -> Journal: Consume session with durable completion receipt
    Guard -> Guard: Apply the saved policy to verified claims if available
    Guard -> Evidence: Record decision and provenance
    alt Evidence recorded
        Guard -> Journal: Acknowledge completion receipt
        Guard --> Caller: Decision ID and outcome
    else Completion interrupted
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · keep the operation blocked
        Caller -> Guard: Repeat the exact completion within 24 hours\nof session creation
        Guard -> Evidence: Reconcile the stored receipt
        alt Decision already recorded
            Guard -> Journal: Acknowledge completion receipt
            Guard --> Caller: HTTP 409 · use scoped export to inspect it
        else No prior decision and storage available
            Guard -> Journal: Acknowledge completion receipt
            Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · indeterminate with decision ID
        else Evidence still unavailable
            Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · evidence_unavailable
        end
    end
else Session expired without a confirmed result
    Guard -> Evidence: Resolve the local expiry decision
    alt Evidence available and expiry eligible
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · wallet_expired
    else Decision retired after evidence pruning
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 409 · wallet_session_conflict
    else Evidence unavailable
        Guard --> Caller: HTTP 503 · evidence_unavailable
    end
end

opt A recorded decision and signed export enabled
    Caller -> Guard: GET /evidence with the same caller,\nendpoint, operationId and exact decisionId
    Guard -> Evidence: Read the caller-scoped decision and sign export
    Guard --> Caller: HTTP 200 · signed JSON evidence
end

note over Guard, Journal
  The recovery receipt stores no raw presentation or plaintext claims.
  After the recovery deadline, a pending receipt retires without a new
  signed decision. Inspect pending receipts before downgrading.
end note
@enduml
